1. INSTALLATION & DIRECTORY PREPARATION:
   - Download and install NXLog Community Edition on the Windows VM.
   - Default installation path: C:\Program Files (x86)\nxlog
   - Inside the NXLog directory, make sure to create a folder named "data" 
     (Path: C:\Program Files (x86)\nxlog\data) so NXLog can write its log files.

2. CONFIGURATION FILE (nxlog.conf):
   - Locate the configuration file at: 
     C:\Program Files (x86)\nxlog\conf\nxlog.conf
   - Replace its contents with the following configuration:

--------------------------------------------------
Root C:\Program Files (x86)\nxlog
LogFile C:\Program Files (x86)\nxlog\data\nxlog.log

<Extension json>
    Module      xm_json
</Extension>

<Input eventlog>
    Module      im_msvistalog
</Input>

<Output udpsender>
    Module      om_udp
    Host        192.168.1.13:10514
    Exec        to_json();
</Output>

<Route 1>
    Path        eventlog => udpsender
</Route>
--------------------------------------------------

3. RUNNING NXLog:
   - Open Command Prompt (CMD) as Administrator.
   - Navigate to the NXLog directory:
     cd "C:\Program Files (x86)\nxlog"
   - Run NXLog in the foreground to verify and send logs:
     nxlog.exe -f

4. RECEIVING & PARSING LOGS (Python Backend):
   - Ensure your Python UDP server is listening on port 10514 (192.168.1.13:10514).
   - Ensure your Python script parses the incoming JSON objects from NXLog 
     properly to store them in your normalized event logs.






